  "welcomeBodyIos": "This app is part of an MSc research project studying mobile network quality of experience. Running quietly in the background, it records the network type and connection quality that iOS makes available, approximate location, and whether a call is in progress - only to tag *when* and *under what conditions* a measurement was taken.\n\nIt never reads message content, browsing history, or anything you type. Over the next few screens we'll ask for the permissions the app needs, and explain exactly why each one is needed before asking.",
  "@welcomeBodyIos": {
    "description": "iOS variant, approved by the owner on 2026-11-11."
  },
  "consentBodyIos": "ABOUT THIS STUDY\n\nQoESense is part of an MSc research project studying how network signal conditions affect real-world app experience, so that quality of experience can eventually be predicted directly from network data. Participation is completely voluntary: you can stop at any time by disabling collection in the app or uninstalling it, with no consequences.\n\nWHAT WE COLLECT ON AN IPHONE\n\n- Network type: whether your iPhone is on 4G (LTE), 5G or an older network, as reported by iOS.\n- Connection info: Wi-Fi vs. cellular, and an estimate of throughput and latency (the time a small test request takes).\n- Approximate location, sampled alongside each network reading, to map coverage along your usual routes.\n- Whether a phone or internet call (for example WhatsApp or FaceTime) is in progress. iOS only tells the app that some call is active - never with whom, through which app, or anything said.\n- Your device model, iOS version, and the app's own version number.\n- Your occasional 1-5 star ratings of network quality and, if you choose to answer, what you were doing at the time (for example \"WhatsApp call\").\n\nWHAT AN IPHONE DOES NOT LET US COLLECT\n\niOS does not give apps the signal strength and quality figures (RSRP, RSRQ, SINR), the cell tower identifier, the roaming status, or which app you are using. This app therefore does not collect them on an iPhone, and never estimates them.\n\nWHAT WE NEVER COLLECT\n\nMessage content, call content, browsing history, photos, contacts, keystrokes, or anything typed into any app - this app has no access to and does not request any of that.\n\nHOW YOUR DATA IS IDENTIFIED\n\nYou are never asked for your name, phone number, or email. Each install gets a random anonymous ID generated by the app, and all your data is tied only to that ID - not to you personally. We have no way to look up who a given ID belongs to from the data alone. Your anonymous ID is shown on the app's Status screen if you ever need to reference it.\n\nWHERE YOUR DATA GOES AND HOW IT'S PROTECTED\n\nData is uploaded only over Wi-Fi (never using your mobile data, a personal hotspot or Low Data Mode), encrypted in transit, and stored on Google Firebase/Cloud infrastructure with access restricted to the research team. Raw data is queued locally on your iPhone and only deleted once a successful upload is confirmed.\n\nHOW YOUR DATA IS USED\n\nYour data will be used to build and evaluate multiple deep learning models for predicting network quality of experience, as part of an MSc research project. Aggregated or de-identified results may be published in academic work; individual raw data will not be shared publicly or with third parties.\n\nPERMISSIONS THIS APP ASKS FOR, AND WHY\n\n- Location (\"While Using the App\", then \"Always\"): used to map network coverage along your routes, and the only way iOS allows an app to keep measuring in the background. While the app collects in the background, iOS shows a location indicator in the status bar.\n- Notifications: used only for the occasional quality-rating prompts, which you can answer directly from the notification.\n\nCOLLECTION ON AN IPHONE HAS GAPS\n\niOS decides when apps may run. Collection can pause - for example if you close the app from the app switcher, turn off its location access, or when iOS stops it to save battery or memory - and resumes when you open the app again or iOS restarts it. Missing periods are kept as gaps: nothing is filled in or estimated.\n\nYOUR RIGHTS\n\nParticipation is voluntary. You can stop data collection at any time from the app's Status screen, or withdraw completely by deleting the app - either way, no further data will be collected from your device. To request that already-uploaded data tied to your device be deleted, contact bilalkouotou@gmail.com with your anonymous device ID from the Status screen.\n\nQUESTIONS OR CONCERNS\n\nThis study is conducted by ENGR. KOUOTOU AHMAD BILAL, from the UNIVERSITY OF BUEA, under THE VICE CHANCELORS' approval. Contact bilalkouotou@gmail.com with any questions.\n\nBy tapping \"I agree, continue\" below, you confirm you've read this and voluntarily agree to participate.",
